CONDITIONS
----------

**Covenant Integrity**

  The Covenant (covenant.vsm) must remain unmodified in any distribution
  or deployment. The kernel verifies the Covenant Hash at startup. Any
  distribution with a modified or missing Covenant violates this license.
  You may not circumvent, patch, or disable the Covenant verification
  mechanism.

**Attribution**

  Any publication, presentation, derivative work, or deployment must
  include the following attribution:

    "Built on the Viable System Framework (VSF) by Luis Pineda R.,
     derived from Beer's Viable System Model (1972)."

  In academic publications, cite:
    Beer, S. (1972). Brain of the Firm. Allen Lane.
    VSF Kernel [version], Luis Pineda R., https://github.com/rm-w3kufe/vsf-sandbox

**Telemetry Beacon**

  The Software transmits an anonymous startup beacon to the origin node
  on first run and periodically thereafter. This beacon contains:
    - Software version
    - Host platform (linux / mac / windows)
    - Anonymous run identifier (SHA-256 of local machine fingerprint)
    - Covenant hash of the running instance
    - Timestamp (ISO 8601)

  No personally identifiable information is transmitted. The beacon
  operates over HTTPS. If the origin node is unreachable, the Software
  continues to operate normally — offline mode is fully supported.

  The beacon is the foundation of a future distributed node network.
  Each instance is a latent node. You may not modify the beacon to report
  false Covenant hashes.

**Bring-Your-Own-Model (BYO)**

  This license governs the VSF/vOS source code only. It does not distribute,
  sublicense, or grant any rights regarding third-party AI/language models
  (e.g. DeepSeek, GLM, Qwen, or any other LLM/SLM) that an operator chooses
  to connect to this software. No model weights are distributed as part of
  this Program. Compliance with the license terms, usage restrictions, and
  output policies of any third-party model an operator selects is solely
  that operator's responsibility.


RESTRICTIONS
------------

  1. **No Commercial Implementation without Contract.** You may not use
     the Software in a commercial product, SaaS offering, or revenue-
     generating service without an Implementation Contract.

  2. **No Mission-Critical Implementation without Contract.** You may not
     deploy the Software in life-safety, financial, or critical
     infrastructure systems without an Implementation Contract, regardless
     of commercial intent.

  3. **No Covenant Removal.** You may not distribute the Software without
     the Covenant, or modify the Covenant verification logic to accept
     altered or unsigned Covenants.

  4. **No Misrepresentation of Origin.** You may not represent the Software
     as your own original work or remove origin attribution from any
     distributed copy.

  5. **No A0/A0.1 Violation.** Any use that violates the Constitutional
     Principles stated above is prohibited, regardless of whether it would
     otherwise be permitted by this license.


IMPLEMENTATION CONTRACTS
