To obtain an Implementation Contract, contact the Author:
  Luis Pineda R. — rmw3kufe@proton.me

Implementation Contracts define the scope of the permitted deployment,
attribution requirements, contribution expectations, telemetry terms, and
commercial terms. Non-profit organizations, universities, and community
projects are encouraged to request contracts — terms are designed to be
accessible.


FUTURE OPEN SOURCE RELEASE
---------------------------

Apache License 2.0 activates automatically when the VSF governance body
is established, as formally specified in covenant.vsm §governance.

The governance body is a foundation, directorate, or equivalent legal
entity with: formal decision-making authority over S5 (covenant + license),
gender equity in composition, multi-disciplinary representation, and at
least 3 active members from distinct institutions.

Establishment must be documented publicly and registered in covenant.vsm
as a version increment. This transition is a design goal, not a concession —
no single person should carry the weight of a system designed to distribute it.

The Covenant and attribution requirements survive any future license change.


